 "rate": {
  "description": "Overall rate normalization. The MaxEnt weight preserves the prior's normalization (sum w = sum w0) and transfers only the shape; K = sigma_calc / sigma_prior sets the absolute scale. Every fitted moment is normalized by the total rate, so K does not enter the fit and changes no normalized distribution. Apply it where the calculation is in control: apply_lambdas multiplies the reweighted branch by K and leaves the generator's tail above the hand-off untouched (rate_tail=True scales every event instead). The total rate of the sample is then K x (bulk) + (tail). Per scheme use per_scheme[s].K with schemes[s] of lambda_export_variations.json.",
